WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.120
[Curtains open]

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:02.740
Good morning, John.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:06.960
I'm here in beautiful Anaheim, California, which you can't see out the window because it's very late.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.680
I'm here for VidCon but I'm going to do all the people who aren't at VidCon a favor and not talk about VidCon.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:16.020
Is that okay? Here's the situation: I don't like flying. I don't like when somebody tells me

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.640
when I can and cannot go to the bathroom. I get nosebleeds, get slightly airsick.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:22.980
I don't like being away from the Internet and the plane smells kind of funny.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.700
But I end up doing it a lot anyway and I kind of feel like I'm getting pretty good at it, so maybe

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.240
there's some wisdom that I can impart to the world.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.440
So, without further ado, here are my 17 tips to make your travel day less terrible.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.240
[Electronic music]

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.200
Don't try and pack everything you might ever possibly need. Make some hard decisions.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.420
I'm going on a three week long trip and this is my bag.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:49.120
Now I know, I don't care that much about this, and yeah, I only own one pair of shoes.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:54.980
But if I can get it into that, then you can get it into one bag. And that's just going to make your life way easier.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:01:00.060
You're not your best self on travel days. You're going to be a little bit tired, maybe stupid, cranky.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:03.840
You might smell kind of bad. That's fine. You have permission to be that way,

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.200
but also: Give everybody else permission to be that way as well.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:08.940
[Electronic music]

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:14.700
Liquids and gels go into this thing. If they don't fit into this thing, then you can't bring them through security.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.880
Peanut butter counts as a gel. I learned this the hard way.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.620
Nowadays, you got to take everything out of your pockets when you go through security.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.200
If you have, like, a tiny piece of paper in your pocket, then the guy at the security will be like,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.340
"Sir, what's in your pocket?" and you'll be like, "Well, on the scanner, it probably looks like a tiny piece of paper,

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.580
but in fact, it is a rocket launcher!"

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:35.340
Which leads me to: Don't be mean to security people, even though it's fun to joke about

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:39.060
because they don't make the rules and they do get fired if they don't enforce them.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:44.220
But, also don't joke with them about your pocket rocket launcher unless you want to eat the carpet.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.300
If you wear a hoodie, you will be pulled aside for further screening. This is not profiling.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:51.020
There's just a lot of room in that thing to hide stuff.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.820
[Electronic music]

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:57.860
If you don't have a big carry-on, you don't need to get on and make sure that it finds a space. Just chill at the gate

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:03.160
You don't need to get in that big, long line. You don't got to jostle for position. You have an assigned seat.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:07.760
You're going to get there eventually and it's going to be less comfortable than the one you're in right now.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:13.680
So just chill until it's like, final boarding and then you just walk on the plane. Love it!

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:20.540
Okay, so you're boarding the plane. Get out of the aisle! This is one artery and if you're clogging it,

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:22.000
everyone's dying.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.360
You may notice that the people in First Class look unhappy and this may seem odd to you,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.840
because you're like, "But they're the First Class people. They got the best seats on the plane."

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:33.660
But it turns out that they got them by travelling like two hundred days a year. They don't pay extra for those.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:38.300
They're like the "super" VIPs because they travel all the time. And that's just no way to live your life.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.160
[Electronic music]

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.380
Depending on the airline, you will get various things for free during your flight, but you can only ever really count

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:49.980
on one of these of some sort and maybe one of these, which are these little Biscoff cookies.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.340
Also, cup of soda, water, juice or coffee, something like that. So maybe bring a snack.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.380
Also, a water bit- Bittle?

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:59.820
A water bottle to fill up after you've gone through security because apparently past security

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.920
is the only place in the world where it's okay to charge five dollars for a bottle of water.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:06.000
So you're not allowed to use electronics during the takeoff and landing because apparently

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:13.040
the fifty millivolts from your Kindle is going to blow up a 747 or something, so bring a real book.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.100
They're great anyway, aren't they nice?

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.940
[Electronic music]

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:20.940
If you have a connecting flight, first thing you do is you go to the board and see where it is and what time it is,

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.700
even if you're like two hours late because that flight may have been delayed, too, and you don't want to miss it

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:26.740
if you don't have to.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:30.840
If you do miss a connection while you're waiting in line to get your stuff rerouted, you can be on Kayak

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.680
or Hipmunk or whatever, looking up to see what flights you might get on, or you can just call the customer

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:39.120
support because it's better to be waiting in two lines if you can do two at the same time.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.280
You never know which one's going to fit it up first. This has helped me many a time.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.260
I hope this video helps you out next time you go on a travel adventure.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.340
John, I will see you on Tuesday.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:50.188
I think I may be seeing you before then, actually, because you're like literally on the other side of that wall.

